I'm trying to implement a similar one-line-installer for my package as https://github.com/rstudio/tensorflow/blob/main/R/install.R
the problem is that py_install doesn't work with system python with method ='auto' (which is selected in case when only Sys python is available)
The current workaround we have looks like that

```  if(method=='auto'){
    python_info <- getAnywhere('python_info')[1]
    py_type <- python_info(py_exe())$type 
    
    if(!is.null(py_type)){
      if(py_type == "system"){
        user_input <- tolower(readline(prompt="method='auto' found only system python, you have to install miniconda to continuue or setup venv manually, enter Y to continue: "))
        if(user_input=='y'){
          reticulate::install_miniconda()
        }else{
          stop('Cannot install XYZ in system python')
        }
      }
        
    }
  }```

but using getAnywhere('python_info')[1] or copying it's content to our package seems like a really bad idea long term.

Would it be possible to export python_info function ? Thanks !

With the recent addition of a default `length()` for python objects, `py_last_error()` is no longer useful in the IDE now if a python object that doesn't define a `len` method is in the active R environment (e.g., a keras model). This is because the IDE calls `length` on objects to populate the environment pane, and that in turn will set the last python exception to "object has no len() method", overwriting whatever exception was actually generated by user code.

Some ideas for how to fix: 
+ Temporarily remove `length.python.builtin.object` method until the the error handling refactoring discussed in #1113 is completed; 
+ add something like a `s_lastError.restore_previous()` method call [here in `py_len_impl`](https://github.com/rstudio/reticulate/blob/21fd315a422a46fd820d7d4bac4426f16072f54c/src/python.cpp#L3042); 
+ do something in the IDE to not call `length` on python objects.

@yihui I believe the change in https://github.com/yihui/knitr/commit/db7345ba1414c75ac0d050598cba965b40a9dce7 for https://github.com/yihui/knitr/issues/1853 will break **reticulate** python engine

Currently it is using the unexported `wrap` function 
https://github.com/rstudio/reticulate/blob/c0d4821ceb596d680700b40f7319c97c7d5a9ff3/R/knitr-engine.R#L455-L461

Exporting the function will help remove this trick, but changing its name will require adaptation. 
@kevinushey I open this issue so that the change that will happen we'll be correctly taken into account here.

