Dear reticulate maintainers,

I needed to find out the version of `pip`. I couldn't find a function to do so in `reticulate`, so I wrote and tested one. I suggest to add such a function to `reticulate`.

I volunteer to add it using a Pull Request. You may also suggest another name as `get_pip_version` if desired.

Cheers, Richel Bilderbeek


```{r}
#' Get the version of pip
#' @export
get_pip_version <- function() {
  line <- system2("python", args = c("-m", "pip", "--version"), stdout = TRUE)
  stringr::str_match(line, "pip (.*) from")[1, 2]
}
```

```{r}
test_that("use", {
  if (!reticulate::py_available()) return()

  version <- get_pip_version()
  expect_equal(1, length(version))
  expect_equal("character", class(version))

})
```

