In RStudio, after 
`   numpy <- import("numpy")`
then numpy functions are all available: in fact, after typing numpy$, the list of all functions shows up, with their signatures. I am using BERT to make functions visible to Excel, and for a normal package, e.g. gsl, this function makes it all:

```
usepkg <- function (pkg) {
  env = as.environment(paste0('package:',pkg ))
  lapply( ls(env,pkg ), function(name){
    newname <- paste0( pkg, '.', name )
    cat(paste0(newname, "\n"))
    func <- get( name, envir=env)
    if( is.function( func )){
      assign( newname, func, .GlobalEnv )
    }
  })
}
```
A call like usepkg("gsl") clones the gsl functions in the global environment, and this make them visible to Excel. Unfortunately, the same for numpy bumps on the first line, _'no item called "package:numpy" on the search list'_.

